# nr-office-ooxml-xlsx-layout-audits: integration fragment

Four modules join the crate mixdog-ooxml (native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml): xlsx_range_layout (sort_range, autofit_range),
xlsx_pivot_ops (add_pivot_table), xlsx_formula_audit (the formula audit of snapshot sheets and its merge into a host result)
and xlsx_assertions (the workbook assertions). No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to this task. None
of the modules compiles until the lines below are applied (nothing was compiled: cargo was not run).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod pivot;` (the last module line), add:

    pub mod xlsx_range_layout;
    pub mod xlsx_pivot_ops;
    pub mod xlsx_formula_audit;
    pub mod xlsx_assertions;

and append to the list of parts in the crate documentation, if the lead keeps it: the range layout, pivot operation, formula
audit and workbook assertions of `portable-xlsx-range-layout.mjs`, `portable-xlsx-pivot-ops.mjs`, `xlsx-formula-audit.mjs` and
`xlsx-assertions.mjs`.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/Cargo.toml

In [dependencies], add (both are existing [workspace.dependencies] entries; mixdog-js already uses them):

    icu_collator = { workspace = true }
    icu_locale_core = { workspace = true }

They give sort_range the collator Node's `Intl.Collator(undefined, { numeric: true, sensitivity: 'base' })` is: the process's
default locale (mixdog_js::default_locale_tag, the same reader localeCompare uses) with the numeric ordering extension and
primary strength. mixdog-js has no such collator entry point, and the vendored icu_collator is the one the workspace resolves
(Cargo.toml [patch]/vendor entry), so no new crate is pulled in.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

The package mixdog-ooxml gains the dependency edges icu_collator and icu_locale_core (both already locked, used by mixdog-js).

