(Check with benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs; the recording is native/core/fixtures/office-xlsx-layout-audits/
golden.json, whose workbooks carry the timestamps of the Node writer, so a re-recording changes its bytes and its sha.)

## What the wiring applies when it connects these (no handler was registered here)

- applyXlsx of the portable writer: the operation table rows `sort_range` -> `xlsx_range_layout::sort_worksheet_range(zip,
  sheet, xml, op)`, `autofit_range` -> `xlsx_range_layout::autofit_worksheet_range(measurer, zip, sheet, xml, op)` and
  `add_pivot_table` -> `xlsx_pivot_ops::add_worksheet_pivot_table(measurer, zip, sheet, xml, op)`. `op` is the operation's
  JSON object; each returns the result object Node returns or the error text Node throws. The measurer is the
  `TextMeasurer` the engine already holds for set_page_setup.
- The quality and finalize reviews: `xlsx_formula_audit::audit_xlsx_formulas(sheets, &AuditOptions { audit_profile,
  sheet_names, defined_names })` (profile `financial-model` turns the modelling discipline on; the other profiles Node names
  run the hygiene alone) and `merge_xlsx_formula_audit(result, document, audit_profile, sheet)` for a host's answer; the
  inputs of quality/assurance-structure-xlsx.mjs and office-actions-inspect.mjs.
- `xlsx_assertions::evaluate_xlsx_assertions(document, assertions)` for portable-validation.mjs; it fails only with the
  SyntaxError text of an assertion whose `matches` is not a regular expression, as Node throws.

Not in any file of this task: the removal of the Node files (portable-xlsx-range-layout.mjs, portable-xlsx-pivot-ops.mjs,
xlsx-formula-audit.mjs, xlsx-assertions.mjs, xlsx-formula-audit.test.mjs) belongs to the deletion task of the office track
once their callers (core/office-actions-inspect.mjs, quality/assurance-structure-xlsx.mjs, portable-validation.mjs,
portable-xlsx.mjs) are ported.
